# Normalise line endings on the way into git.
#
# The repo lives on an NTFS path reached from WSL, so tools on either side write
# whichever ending they prefer and analysis/census/*.json|csv have shown up as
# fully-modified in `git status` ever since -- 4805/4805 lines changed, with
# `git diff --ignore-all-space` empty. That churn hides real edits and makes
# every diff review start by discarding noise.
#
# `text=auto` stores LF in the object database and leaves working-tree endings
# to core.autocrlf. Existing files are only renormalised when next written; to
# do it now, run:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#
* text=auto

# Explicit for the files that actually churned.
*.json  text
*.csv   text
*.yaml  text
*.yml   text
*.md    text
*.py    text
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.usd   binary
*.hdf5  binary
*.parquet binary
*.zip   binary
